33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The monitors show a huge gap. One room uses four times more than another. It is mostly heaters.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,I saw how long the other house takes. Forty minutes a month just to log it. Plus the arguments.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The sunlight data confirms it. Two rooms are cold in winter. The others are warm. The lot was unfair.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The statements show wild swings. February is nearly three times August. A flat rate is impossible.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,The kitchen notice is still up. People are sweating to avoid the bill. It is affecting our health.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, so the physical setup is the problem. We need to account for the cold rooms.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, if the swings are that big, a seasonal fixed rate might be the only way to stop the shock.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, yes. But we also need to know the cost of installing meters. It might be too high.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I agree. But the reconciliation template is a nightmare. Keying in every invoice is too much work.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, if it takes forty minutes, that is a lot of time. Can we automate it?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The electrician quote is 34,000 yen per room. That is 170,000 yen total. Plus annual checks.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that is a lot of money. But if it stops the arguments, maybe it is worth it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I am not sure. The trial run of the template was painful. I don't want to do that every year.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, the template is for a flat share. If we use meters, we don't need the complex reconciliation.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,I think we should try the meters. It feels fairer. I don't want to feel guilty about the heater.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am leaning towards meters. It solves the comfort issue and the fairness issue.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I am worried about the time. But if we use a simple app, maybe it is manageable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Benjamin. The data is clear. The current system is broken.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I am still concerned about the upfront cost. But the seasonal swings are too big for a flat rate.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I will support the meters. I want us to be happy here.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
